# SYNTHESISED to exercise a span whose start was clamped to zero. Unlike
# every other timeline fixture here, the first line is NOT an anchor placed
# far enough back to keep every start unclamped -- it sits only 2s before
# the first response, which reports a 45s duration. ReportedBuilder cannot
# subtract 45s from a 2s offset, so it clamps that span's start to zero and
# records StartClamped (see the doc comment on span.Span). The span's bar is
# therefore drawn from column 0 and only 2s long, beside a detail pane
# reading 45.0s: the positional distortion the timeline's clamped-start note
# exists to declare. A second, ordinary aws call closes at 12s so the log
# also carries an unclamped span to contrast with, and the 5s window between
# the two carries no call at all. The line shape is
# testdata/two-providers.log's "Received downstream response" verbatim.
# Values are invented; no line here is from a real run.
